2026-11-12T10:53:10.6578593Z """Dataset "top": several current top-of-ladder strategies as teachers, each on its own style row, whole games.
2026-11-12T10:53:10.6579958Z Why: one teacher's games are few for a 3M-parameter net (Master3s: ~120 games); the other strong players' games teach
2026-11-12T10:53:10.6581401Z the trunk the same board situations (trees under contest, crowded bases, fights for cargo) from several hands, while
2026-11-12T10:53:10.6582430Z the style row keeps whose decisions are whose.
2026-11-12T10:53:10.6583354Z   python3 build_top.py OUT_DIR REPLAY_DIR [REPLAY_DIR ...]    then    python3 set_uw.py OUT_DIR 1 1 1
2026-11-12T10:53:10.6584667Z Teachers: the default set (J1, five teachers, rows 2-6), or CNET2_TOP=J2 (eight teachers, all rows), or an explicit
2026-11-12T10:53:10.6586043Z CNET2_TOP_TEACHERS="name@row,name@row,..." (rows 0-7; names exactly as on the leaderboard).
2026-11-12T10:53:10.6587340Z Master3s stays on row 2 in every set -- the row the Echo packs play.
2026-11-12T10:53:10.6588366Z Only ladder replays (public games) -- never games generated locally with someone's public source."""
